# Peano addition (ExamplePeano.addProgram in the Arend project): 1 + 3 on unary
# naturals.
#
# Arend-authored: prog.ast is `ExamplePrint:peanoSexpr` serialized by
# Serialize.ard and regenerated by test/tools/regen-arend-asts.sh. This file is
# byte-identical to the one the retired `peano-ast` case checked in, which is
# exactly why that case no longer needs to exist: the round trip is now the only
# path to the program.
#
# The result is constructor DATA, not a scalar, and our Java renderer prints it
# multi-line with per-level indentation; see ../example/meta. The expected value
# is derived from the Arend source by hand: `Nat` is declared zero then suc, so
# zero = 0 and suc = 1, and 1 + 3 = suc^4 zero = 1(1(1(1(0)))). run.py deletes
# whitespace before comparing, so the indentation does not appear here.
expected=1(1(1(1(0))))
backends=java
runtime=
xfail=
note=1+3 = suc^4 zero; our Java printer renders it as a multi-line 1(1(1(1(0))))
